y 08:00-12:00, 16:00-20:00","","","","r","Easily spotted from the Corniche with its distinctive spiral minaret, the center aims to educate non-Muslims about Islam by offering free Arabic classes as well as art and calligraphy exhibits. The center conducts bi-weekly tours of…"],["Clock Tower","sight",25.29002,51.52897,"","","","","","r","Next to the Grand Mosque, this old clock tower features Arabic numerals on its face. The tower is also on a hill, and as such offers some wonderful views of the Corniche."],["Windtower House","sight",25.28554,51.53333,"Grand Hamad St & Ali bin Abdulla St","","","","","r","One of the last traditional windtowers in Qatar. Windtowers were used in the days before air conditioning, functioning by sucking cool air into a house. The house is not open to the public, but can be viewed from the outside."],["Souq Waqif","sight",25.2884,51.5329,"","Closed for lunch 12:30-15:30","","","","r","Souq Waqif is the renovated Arabic market quarter, where one can easily wander around the maze-like corridors for hours. The souq is organized more or less by what is sold. There is a section of spice shops, another of textiles, and…"],["Al Najada","sight",25.28353,51.53351,"","","","","","r","For a glimpse of some older Qatari architecture, it can be worthwhile to wander around some of the older neighborhoods surrounding Souq Waqif, particularly the small neighborhood to the immediate south of the souq. There are still a few…"],["Corniche","sight",25.2945,51.5239,"","","","","","r","The visual highlight of Doha is Al-Corniche, a long seaside promenade that curves around Doha Bay and affords pretty views of Palm Tree Island and the city's skyscrapers. In the afternoons you will see plenty of locals strolling, often…"],["Al Hamra","restaurant",25.28855,51.52173,"Al Rayan Rd","06:00-01:00 daily","","","","r","A family restaurant offering Lebanese dishes. Service is a bit slow, good for large groups."],["Shay Al Shoomos","restaurant",25.28965,51.53273,"Souq Waqif","","","","","r","A popular breakfast spot, and one of the few very few places that serves traditional Qatari cuisine."]]}